                <pb facs="d331-02" n="2" xml:id="d331-02"/>


                <head>Letter From President Nixon to President Nimeri</head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date when="1972-07-29">July 29,
                        1972</date></dateline>
                <p>Dear Mr. President:</p>
                <p>I would like to express to you my deep gratification in the resumption of
                    diplomatic relations between Sudan and the United States. The United States has
                    always had a deep interest in Sudan as the largest of the African states with
                    important historic and cultural ties with the Arab world as well. During the
                    past two years I have followed with great personal interest your statesmanship
                    in establishing cordial relations between Sudan and its neighbors and your
                    leadership in achieving the reconciliation of the Sudanese people.</p>
                <p>On this historic occasion in the relations between our two governments, I would
                    like to assure you that the United States will continue to follow with sympathy
                    your efforts to realize the full potential of Sudan and the Sudanese people. The
                    United States is willing to do what it can to assist in those efforts.</p>
                <pb facs="d331-03" n="3" xml:id="d331-03"/>
                <p>Please accept, Mr. President, my warmest best wishes to you, which I ask you to
                    extend on behalf of the American people to the people of Sudan.</p>
                <closer>Sincerely, <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        Richard Nixon
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
